'''Callejón railway station''' ({{lang-bl|Estación de la Callejón}}) is a major through [[W:Train station|station]] recently completed in the [[Limón]] borough in the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. It is intended to serve as the central station for northern and eastern Castejón, with [[Coruxón station|Coruxón]] serving as the central station for southern and southeastern Castejón, and [[Hisbanya Station]] for the west. 

Together with [[Hisbanya railway station|Hisbanya]] and Coruxón it is one of the three high-speed rail stations within the Metropolis, and it serves the [[Atlantic Axis high-speed rail line|Atlantic Axis]] and [[Las Viñas high speed rail line|Las Viñas]] high-speed rail lines. It will also be on the conventional [[Cisalpujarra railway|''Cisalpujarra'']] and [[South Atlantic Railway|''Atlántico Sur'']] railways. It is built to be a major public transport hub, with dedicated stations on [[Castejón Metro]] lines [[Castejón Metro Excursión Line|3]], [[Line 9 (Castejón Metro)|9]] and [[Castejón Metro Arrayanes Line|11]], as well as a [[W:Bus station|bus station]]. The complex is fully underground except for the station building, with two levels of platforms, accounting for a total of 18 railway tracks. 

